    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "THE QUESTION",
      "estimated_duration_s": 9.0,
      "narration_text": "A drug reaches the tumor. Vessels are leaky and particles accumulate. The outer rim is cleared. Weeks later, the tumor regrows from the inside. The drug was there. Why did the core survive?",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "hold"
      },
      "scene_class": "B03_Question",
      "audio_file": "../vox-tumor-pressure/mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.773,
      "locked": true,
      "source_clip": "../vox-tumor-pressure/clips/B03.mp4",
      "source_audio": "../vox-tumor-pressure/mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-30T20:22:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "THE PROBLEM",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11.0,
      "narration_text": "The naive picture: leaky vessels let particles in, and particles spread inward through the tissue. That is not wrong — it is just half the story. The same leaky vessels create a second effect no one celebrates.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "reveal"
      },
      "scene_class": "B04_LeakyVessels",
      "audio_file": "../vox-tumor-pressure/mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.691,
      "locked": true,
      "source_clip": "../vox-tumor-pressure/clips/B04.mp4",
      "source_audio": "../vox-tumor-pressure/mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-30T20:22:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "THE PROBLEM",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10.0,
      "narration_text": "Leaky vessel walls pour fluid into the tumor faster than the lymphatic system can drain it. Tumor lymphatics are broken or absent. The fluid has nowhere to go — so it stays, and pressure builds.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "drawon"
      },
      "scene_class": "B05_PressureBuilds",
      "audio_file": "../vox-tumor-pressure/mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.115,
      "locked": true,
      "source_clip": "../vox-tumor-pressure/clips/B05.mp4",
      "source_audio": "../vox-tumor-pressure/mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-30T20:22:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "THE MECHANISM",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12.0,
      "narration_text": "Fluid moves down pressure gradients. The tumor core accumulates fluid and reaches pressures five to ten times higher than normal tissue. Net flow is outward — from the pressurized core toward the tumor edge. A particle trying to move inward is swimming against that current.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "trace"
      },
      "scene_class": "B06_PressureFlow",
      "audio_file": "../vox-tumor-pressure/mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.763,
      "locked": true,
      "source_clip": "../vox-tumor-pressure/clips/B06.mp4",
      "source_audio": "../vox-tumor-pressure/mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-30T20:22:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "act": "THE MECHANISM",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11.0,
      "narration_text": "So particles extravasate near the rim vessels, and the outward current carries them back. They pile up at the periphery. The core stays particle-free — not because the EPR effect failed, but because it succeeded and then the pressure it created pushed the particles away.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "trace"
      },
      "scene_class": "B07_ParticlesPushedBack",
      "audio_file": "../vox-tumor-pressure/mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.869,
      "locked": true,
      "source_clip": "../vox-tumor-pressure/clips/B07.mp4",
      "source_audio": "../vox-tumor-pressure/mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-30T20:22:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "act": "THE IMPLICATION",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11.0,
      "narration_text": "That unreached core is also hypoxic — starved of oxygen. Hypoxia selects for cells that tolerate stress, evade death signals, and survive. The cells the drug never reached are not a random sample. They are the tumor's most resistant survivors.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "reveal"
      },
      "scene_class": "B08_HypoxicCore",
      "audio_file": "../vox-tumor-pressure/mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.315,
      "locked": true,
      "source_clip": "../vox-tumor-pressure/clips/B08.mp4",
      "source_audio": "../vox-tumor-pressure/mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-30T20:22:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "act": "THE IMPLICATION",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10.0,
      "narration_text": "The rim cells the drug killed were not the cells most likely to cause recurrence. The core cells it never reached were — and the hypoxic pressure had spent months making them harder to kill.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "DOCUMENT",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "highlight"
      },
      "scene_class": "B09_InsideOutQuote",
      "audio_file": "../vox-tumor-pressure/mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.453,
      "locked": true,
